📄 Log and File Analysis Commands
Used to inspect logs and search for specific events.
grep
Searches for matching text patterns.
Bash
grep "error" /var/log/syslog
Variants
egrep (supports extended regular expressions)
grep -i (case-insensitive)
grep -r (recursive search)
tail -f
Displays the last lines of a file and follows updates in real time.
Bash
tail -f /var/log/syslog
Use Cases
Monitor live logs
Watch service activity
journalctl
Views logs managed by systemd.
Bash
journalctl
Useful Options
Bash
journalctl -xe        # Detailed errors
journalctl -u ssh     # Logs for SSH service
journalctl -f         # Follow logs live
journalctl -k         # Kernel logs
